course: dictionary
lesson: 12161
title: Formal words in rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Comply means to do what a rule, law, order or request says. «Everyone must comply with the school rules.» The rules tell you what to do, and to comply is to do it.
explain: Comply is a formal word, so you will see it on signs, in letters from school and in safety notices. «Passengers must comply with the seat belt rule.» This means they must follow the rule, even if they would rather not.
explain: Sometimes people do not want to obey. «The boy refused to comply and kept playing on the wet floor.» In stories, comply often tells you that someone obeyed, but not happily. Look for the small words that come after it, such as comply with.
fact: Comply is a verb: comply, complies, complied, complying.
fact: «Comply» means to do what a rule, law, order or request says.
fact: «Comply with» something means to obey it or meet its standard.
fact: Toys and buildings must comply with safety standards, so they are safe to use.
fact: Refuse to comply means you will not obey, and fail to comply means you did not obey.
exercise: «Everyone must comply with the school rules.» What does comply mean? | Write the rule on the board | Break the rule on purpose | *Do what the rule says | Forget the rule
exercise: Which phrase means someone will not obey? | Complied happily | Complying well | Comply with the order | *Refuse to comply
exercise: Ellie's bike must comply with safety standards. What does this mean? | It must be kept in the shed | *It must meet the safety standards | It must be sold quickly | It must be painted red
test: «The bus driver asked everyone to comply with the seat belt rule.» What does comply mean here? | *Obey | Forget | Argue with | Ignore
test: Mia did not comply with the sign on the door. What does this tell you? | She read the sign aloud | *She did not obey the sign | She painted the sign | She played with the sign
exam: Which word is the past tense of comply? | Complying | *Complied | Complain | Complies
